-- @@ L9-22 verbatim
/-!
# Subalgebras of `K[X]` are contained in `K[s]` for a polynomial `s` (via Lüroth)

Let `K` be algebraically closed and `R ⊆ K[X]` a `K`-subalgebra containing a non-constant
polynomial. Then there is a non-constant polynomial `s` in the fraction field of `R` with
`R ⊆ K[s]` (`RatFuncPoly.exists_poly_generator`).

By Lüroth, the subfield of `K(X)` generated by `R` is `K(g)`. After a Möbius change of `g`, the
numerator of `g` has larger degree than its denominator. If `A(g)/B(g)` is a polynomial `P`
(with `A`, `B` coprime), then `B` is constant: otherwise a root `β` of `B` is a value `g(x₁)` at
a point where `g` is finite, and `P(x₁) B(β) = A(β)` forces a common root. If moreover the
denominator of `g` vanished at some `x₀`, then `q^{deg A} P = q^{deg A} A(n/q)` evaluated at `x₀`
forces `deg A = 0`; so a non-constant `P` forces `g` to be a polynomial.
-/


